   GUATEMALA, MAY 08-10, 2024},
Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {In this study, we use various extraction techniques to analyze the
   polarity of economic topics sourced from Mexican news outlets. For this,
   we constructed a comprehensive daily dataset spanning eighteen years,
   covering a diverse range of topics. Following a standard data cleaning
   process, we utilized Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) to identify main
   economic-related concept. Subsequently, we applied a combination of
   rule-based, lexicon-based, and pre-trained language models to determine
   the polarity and sentiment tone from sentences or document level. To
   assess the effectiveness of our sentiment approach, we explored
   traditional word representation, including Word2vec, GloVe, and FastText
   integrated into a Multilayer Perceptron classifier (MLP). Finally, we
   examine the relationship between the derived sentiment index and the
   Consumer Price Index (CPI). We observe that the lexicon achieved higher
   precision (88.39\%), outperforming the other word embedding techniques.},
