Abstract = {Electric power load forecasting is very important for the operation and
   the planning of a utility company. Decisions of the electric market,
   electric power generation, load switching, and infrastructure
   development depend on load forecasting. There are many methods for load
   forecasting using statistical models, machine learning models and hybrid
   models. In this work, a Long-Short Term Memory Neural Network (LSTM NN)
   is used for short-term load forecasting, ranging from 1 h to 2 h ahead.
   Electric power demand time series provided by the National Center of
   Energy Control (CENACE) is used to train and validate the network.
   Results are compared with reported values from CENACE and Mean Absolute
   Percentage Errors (MAPEs) are calculated.},
