Month = {MAR},
Abstract = {In this note we study a conjecture by Jeronimo-Castro, Magazinov and
   Soberon which generalized a question posed by Dol'nikov. Let F1, F2,
   ..., Fn be families of translates of a convex compact set K in the plane
   so that each two sets from distinct families intersect. We show that,
   for some j, ui =j Fi can be pierced by at most 4 points. To do so, we
   use previous ideas from Gomez-Navarro and Roldan-Pensado together with
   an approximation result closely tied to the Banach-Mazur distance to the
   square.(c) 2023 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.},
